{"https://yugiohblog.konami.com/2017/championships/welcome-to-the-south-american-wcq/":[{"t":"p","r":["Welcome to the 2017 South American WCQ!"]},{"t":"p","r":["We’ve got a total of 278 Duelists for the Main Event and here are the country breakdowns: 38 Duelists from Argentina, 5 from Bolivia, 27 from Chile, 6 from Colombia, 3 from Ecuador, 1 from Paraguay, 11 from Peru, 1 from Uruguay and 2 from Venezuela. The remaining 184 Duelists are from Brazil. Welcome everyone, Duel hard but have fun!"]}],"https://yugiohblog.konami.com/2017/ycs/top-cut-for-dragon-duel-at-the-south-american-wcq-2/":[{"t":"p","r":["Here are the talented 4 Dragon Duelists returning tomorrow to try and win the Title of South American Dragon Duel Champion, and a trip to Japan to compete for the Dragon Duel World Championship title!"]},{"t":"p","r":["In 4th place: ",{"who":"Johan Daniel Argamarca","t":"Johan Daniel Argamarca"}," from Ecuador (2017 Dragon Duel National Champion), with his Zoodiac Deck. in 3rd place: ",{"who":"Rafael Mariano Reich","t":"Rafael Mariano Reich"}," from Brazil (2017 Dragon Duel National Champion), with his Zoodiac Deck In 2nd place: ",{"who":"Luciano Daniel Lossio","t":"Luciano Daniel Lossio"}," from Peru (2017 Dragon Duel National Champion), with his True Draco Zoodiac Deck. In 1st place: ",{"who":"Agustin Alonso Mallea","t":"Agustin Alonso Mallea"}," from Chile (2017 Dragon Duel National Champion), with his True Draco Zoodiac Deck."]},{"t":"p","r":["Congratulations to the four of you and see you tomorrow for the Top Cut!"]}],"https://yugiohblog.konami.com/2017/championships/the-finals-have-begun-at-the-south-american-wcq-2/":[{"t":"p","r":["We are now in the Finals of the South American World Championship Qualifier! Will it be Rafael Jose Rodrigues from Brazil or ",{"who":"Kanaan Asfour Al Jaubri","t":"Kanaan Asfour Al Jaubri"},", the Venezuelan National Champion and YCS Bogota Champion ? Both Duelists are using Zoodiac Decks!"]},{"t":"p","r":[{"who":"Rafael Jose Rodri